**Fixed** in `e185d9e354` — exactly the suggested patch shape.

`FileStreamTraceSink`'s constructor now best-effort creates the parent directory before truncating, inside the existing swallow-never-throw try/catch (same pattern as `FileAgentTelemetrySink.record`):

```dart
try {
  _file.parent.createSync(recursive: true);
  _file.writeAsStringSync('', flush: true);
} catch (_) {
  // A broken trace path never breaks the host.
}
```

So on a fresh install / fresh `$HOME` / ephemeral container — where `bin/fah.dart` arms the trace at the top of `main()` before anything has created `~/.fah/logs/` — the trail is actually written instead of silently void.

TDD: `test/providers/stream_trace_io_test.dart` gained `creates a missing parent directory — fresh installs record the trail`, which constructs the sink against a not-yet-created nested path and asserts the marked line lands in the file. It failed before the fix (constructor truncate threw → swallowed → zero bytes) and passes after.
